  "strategy": "Inequality minimization with step-function coefficients requires a deeper understanding of the autocorrelation properties. After re-examining the problem, we realize that the previous Adam optimizer approach wasn't optimal because it only considered candidates within the accepted range (score < 1.5) for further refinement, potentially missing better solutions. We need a more comprehensive technique that evaluates all sequences without such filtering.\n\nOur new approach will use the <direction_optimize> function based on linear programming and updates the global optimum more frequently. Unlike the Adam optimizer, it won't filter candidates and will update throughout the search. This ensures all sequences get the chance to improve the global solution incrementally.\n\nThe evaluation function is f(seq) = 2*n*max(convolve(seq, mode='full')) / (sum(seq))^2. We'll minimize this over all sequences (not just those below 1.5 threshold) by:\n\n1. Starting by <call_order_optimize> on a normalized sequence or using existing best_by_n candidates.\n2. Iteratively updating the sequence using linear programming that maximizes sum(g) subject to ||f*g|| _infty<= M and g>=0.\n   The rationale here is that this cutting-plane method finds sequences where the autocorrelation is concentrated and avoids pathological samples by direct validation.\n3. Running the optimization for each sequence length until improvement stalls.\n4. Including a fallback if linear programming isn't available during phase 2.\n\nThe key is to balance the time between different lengths and represent sequences explicitly (not normalized) during optimization to maintain the gradient property.\n\nFor implementation:\n\n- <call_order_optimize> now includes length-specific budget allocations to speed up important phases for longer sequences.\n- We'll maintain best_by_n as a record.\n- After the optimization phase, we'll scale candidates to have sum >=0.01 and clamp values to [0,1000] for safe evaluation.\n- A global termination time ensures we exit gracefully if 1800 seconds are reached.",
